libstdc++ 13 <format>: std::format("{}", 42) is converted without dropping a
system-header body.  The verification (test_format.desc) is THOROUGH.
With libstdc++ 16 (16-20260315) the test passes: the drops of
<format>'s _Seq_sink::_M_reserve and _M_span were fixed with
cpp20_hidden_friend_spaceship_template_alias_return_type (it was tagged
broken-libstdcxx16).
